39:10.040 --> 39:14.500
I wonder when I got in the habit of
writing messages to nobody?

39:51.830 --> 39:54.290
Kanae, have you decided 
what you'll be doing in the future?

39:54.290 --> 39:57.000
Nope. Like I thought, I'm still not sure...

39:57.000 --> 40:01.750
But it's all right! I decided that I'll just take things on one at a time.

40:01.750 --> 40:02.670
Off I go!

40:20.310 --> 40:24.190
Since that day, a number of typhoons have passed through...

40:24.490 --> 40:28.110
...and the island's become a little cooler each time.

40:30.120 --> 40:33.580
The wind blowing through 
the sugarcane has taken on a slight chill...

40:33.580 --> 40:35.870
...and the sky seems a little higher.

40:35.870 --> 40:38.420
The edges of the clouds have become gentler...

40:38.420 --> 40:43.250
...and my classmates have begun wearing light jackets
when riding their bikes with the change in the weather.

40:58.350 --> 41:01.810
By the time I managed to ride the waves again,
six long months had passed.

41:01.810 --> 41:07.240
Even though it was the middle of October, it felt
like a little bit of summer had been left behind.

41:17.330 --> 41:22.500
The weather forecast for tonight shows a clear evening
with winds up to eight meters per second.

41:21.960 --> 41:25.250
So I heard that Yamada confessed to Sasaki.

41:25.250 --> 41:26.760
No surprise there.

41:27.090 --> 41:29.630
Huh? Kanae, you seem awfully happy today.

41:29.630 --> 41:31.640
Something good happen between you and Tohno?

41:33.010 --> 41:33.930
No way!

41:35.600 --> 41:39.600
Today, I'm finally going to confess to Tohno, too.

41:44.820 --> 41:47.150
If I don't tell him today, 
on the day I finally rode the waves again...

41:47.150 --> 41:50.030
{i1}...I'm sure l won't ever be able to.

42:00.620 --> 42:01.750
Sumida.

42:01.750 --> 42:02.460
Toh—

42:03.830 --> 42:05.000
Tohno.

42:05.460 --> 42:06.250
On your way home?

42:06.250 --> 42:06.960
Yeah.

42:07.550 --> 42:08.340
I see.

42:08.340 --> 42:10.420
Then, let's go home together.

42:33.160 --> 42:35.740
Huh, Sumida? Decided already today?

42:35.740 --> 42:36.490
Yeah.

42:47.920 --> 42:48.630
What's the matter?

42:56.140 --> 42:57.430
...to me...

43:00.020 --> 43:01.430
No... I'm sorry. It's nothing.

43:01.430 --> 43:03.310
No... I'm sorry. It's nothing.

43:11.610 --> 43:12.900
Is your bike acting up?

43:12.900 --> 43:14.860
Yeah... that's kind of weird.

43:16.320 --> 43:17.200
Is it broken?

43:17.200 --> 43:20.330
Yeah... I think the spark plug's dead.

43:20.740 --> 43:21.910
Was this a hand-me-down?

43:21.910 --> 43:23.290
Yeah. It was my sister's.

43:23.290 --> 43:25.080
Did it stall when you tried accelerating?

43:25.080 --> 43:26.580
It might have, actually...

43:27.540 --> 43:29.540
Let's leave it here for today.

43:29.540 --> 43:32.170
You can have someone from your house pick it up later.

43:32.170 --> 43:33.470
Let's walk back today.

43:33.470 --> 43:35.880
Huh? I'll walk by myself!

43:35.880 --> 43:37.680
You go on ahead.

43:37.680 --> 43:39.810
We're far out and your place is nearby.

43:39.810 --> 43:42.430
And... I kind of want to walk today.

44:18.140 --> 44:20.850
Tohno, please...

44:31.940 --> 44:32.820
What's wrong?

44:32.820 --> 44:33.980
I'm sorry...

44:34.820 --> 44:36.190
It's nothing.

44:36.190 --> 44:37.150
I'm so sorry...

44:39.780 --> 44:40.740
Sumida...

44:42.910 --> 44:45.700
I'm begging you... please...

44:45.700 --> 44:49.210
...don't be so nice to me!

46:23.890 --> 46:28.010
As we humans desperately and recklessly
stretched our arms to the top of the sky...

46:28.010 --> 46:31.020
...and launched something of that mass and size into the air...

46:31.020 --> 46:34.730
...gazing off into the distance towards something
far beyond our wildest dreams...

46:39.690 --> 46:45.780
...I felt like I somewhat came to understand why
Tohno was different from the other boys.

46:45.780 --> 46:47.700
And at the same time...

46:47.700 --> 46:53.870
I clearly realized that Tohno wasn't really looking at me.

46:58.090 --> 47:02.510
Which is why, on that day, 
I couldn't say a word to Tohno.

47:16.350 --> 47:18.690
Tohno is really kind, but...

47:18.690 --> 47:20.820
He's so truly kind, but...

47:22.280 --> 47:26.910
But Tohno was always looking far beyond me.

47:26.910 --> 47:30.450
Far beyond me, towards something in the distance.

47:40.420 --> 47:44.260
I'm sure I wouldn't be able 
to give Tohno what he truly desires.

47:44.720 --> 47:48.220
But still... despite that...

47:48.220 --> 47:51.810
Tomorrow, the day after, and even beyond that...

47:51.810 --> 47:54.600
...I know I'll still be helplessly in love with him.

47:57.270 --> 48:03.110
While thinking solely of Tohno, I cried myself to sleep.

48:03.440 --> 48:24.510
“Story Two: Cosmonaut”

48:03.440 --> 48:24.510
End

